      "description": "The BJP and Shiromani Akali Dal are likely to announce their alliance for the upcoming Punjab Assembly polls here on Tuesday.\nThe announcement is likely to be made by Union Home Minister Amit Shah, BJP national president Nitin Nabin and SAD president Sukhbir Singh Badal at the BJP headquarters here at 1 pm.\nNegotiations on seat-sharing between the BJP and the Shiromani Akali Dal (SAD) for the 2027 Punjab Assembly polls have been underway.\nThe SAD had snapped its 24-year-old alliance with the BJP in September 2020 over the now-scrapped three farm laws.\nEarlier, Lok Sabha MP Harsimrat Kaur Badal was also part of the Modi government as a minister with Cabinet rank.\nLast month in Delhi, Shah had predicted an NDA government in Punjab in 2027. When he came to Chandigarh on November 1, he again said an NDA government will be formed in the border state.\nThe statement reignited the buzz about a possible SAD-BJP alliance.\nOn November 2, when SAD president Badal was asked about the possibi",
